@node Top
@top Tweeta Desktop

@insertcopying

Tweeta Desktop is a native GTK3 client for the Tweeta/Tweetapus social
platform.  It is written in C and uses libcurl for HTTP, json-glib for JSON,
GPGME for encrypted messaging support, and optionally libfido2 for native
passkey registration and login.

This manual is the canonical user, administrator, packager, and developer
reference for the desktop client.  It covers installation, daily use, account
features, moderation and administration, local storage, build targets,
architecture, testing, troubleshooting, and the documentation build.

This Texinfo manual replaces the older Markdown documentation tree, which has
been removed.  Keep user-facing, administrator-facing, packager-facing, and
developer-facing documentation here so the Info, PDF, single-page HTML, and
multi-page HTML outputs remain complete and consistent.

@strong{Platform support:} the supported runtime target is Linux.  Other
systems may compile in limited situations, but runtime support outside Linux is
not guaranteed.

