@end table

@node Network Configuration
@chapter Network Configuration

@section Default Server

The compiled defaults are:

@table @code
@item API_BASE_URL
@url{https://tweeta.tiago.zip/api}

@item BASE_DOMAIN
@url{https://tweeta.tiago.zip}
@end table

Runtime environment variables can override both without recompilation.

@section HTTP Behavior

Networking uses libcurl.  Requests include a Tweeta Desktop user agent and an
@code{X-Tweetapus-Client} header.  Authenticated requests include a bearer
token when a session is active.

The networking layer handles ordinary GET-style requests, JSON request bodies,
multipart/media upload helper flows, and challenge retry behavior where the
server requires a CAP challenge token.

@section API Areas

The client integrates with endpoints for:

@itemize @bullet
@item Authentication, passkeys, account validation, delegates, and profile
settings.
@item Public, following, profile, community, list, search, explore, article,
and scheduled-post timelines.
@item Post creation, editing, deletion, interactions, reactions, polls, notes,
outline generation, and bulk deletion.
@item Bookmarks, notifications, direct messages, message attachments, invites,
roles, pinned messages, and disappearing messages.
@item Communities, members, join requests, invites, style, moderation, and
community timelines.
@item Blocking, muting, muted words, muted conversations, and reports.
@item Shop, payments, payment requests, and purchases.
@item Administration for stats, users, posts, reports, logs, DMs, shop,
communities, badges, emojis, notifications, clone-user tools, impersonation,
post-as-user, and bulk edits.
@end itemize

@node Build and Documentation Targets
@chapter Build and Documentation Targets

@section Primary Make Targets

